=== Compare Repair

The compare and repair screen submits and monitors requests for comparison and optionally repairs data between source and target nodes.
Requests sync between nodes and are processed by the <<Compare Job>>.
The following features are supported with comparison:

* Table with a primary key, unique index, or sync key names
* Excluded or included column names, configured by capture or specified transform
* Table with a natural key can be used while ignoring surrogate and foreign keys
* Subsets if the table routing is configured with an initial load select
* Transforms that rename column names

The following features are NOT supported with comparison:

* Tables without a way to uniquely identify a row
* Transforms or filters that modify data
* Subsets without an initial load select

.Panel Controls

Compare Data:: Click button to use a wizard dialog to request a compare operation.
Resubmit:: Select a completed request and click button to copy request into a new request.
Cancel:: Select a running request and click button to stop running and cancel it.
Active Only:: Enable checkbox to filter the view for requests that are submitted or running.
Auto Refresh:: Enable checkbox to update the view of requests periodically with the latest status information.

==== Compare Wizard

The compare wizard dialog builds a request for comparison between a source and target node for all tables or select tables.

image::images/manage/compare-wizard.png[]

.Required Fields

Row counts:: Use row counts to determine if tables match, which is faster but doesn't compare rows.
Row checksums:: Use checksums on the data to determine if tables match, which is slower but more accurate.
Scale for decimals:: Limit the number of digits to the right of the decimal point for comparison of decimal types.
Scale for timestamps:: Limit the number of digits to the right of the decimal point on fractional seconds for comparison of timestamps.
Digits for floating points:: Limit the number of digits to the right of the decimal point for comparison of floating point types.
Use in-flight data:: Enable for a busy system to exclude outstanding data to sync from comparison.
Use chunking:: Enable for efficient use of the network by working with chunks of a table instead of sending all rows for comparison.
Checksum algorithm:: Algorithm that summarizes data to check if data matches.
CRC32 is a trusted data hash algorithm.
PureJavaCrc32 is a Java native implementation of CRC32 that may be 1.8 to 10 times faster with small pieces of data.
Adler32 is slightly faster than CRC32 but has a higher chance of collisions.
XXHash32 is 10 times faster than CRC32 and more resistant to collisions.
Exclude surrogate keys:: Enable for tables with natural keys that should be compared while surrogate keys should be excluded.
The natural key must have a unique index or be configured as sync key names.
Primary and foreign key columns are considered surrogates that are excluded from comparison.
Immediately or schedule:: Run the request immediately or schedule for a future date and time.
Action to take:: Select an action to report and optionally repair data.

[cols="1,6", options="header"]
|===
|Action
|Description

|Level 1 report| Only reports whether or not each table matched without any further statistics.

|Level 2 report| For each table, reports on the row counts that are matching, different, missing, or extra.

|Level 3 report| In addition to the above, provides a script of differences that apply as insert, update, or delete.

|Repair data| In addition to the above, applies the script to repair the data.

|===
